# Tests for the Student_loan_adjustment module (issue #24)

Run with `clerk test`. Hand-worked TY2024 cases from the Student Loan Interest
Deduction Worksheet (`i1040gi--2024.pdf` p 94) and Rev. Proc. 2023-34 § 3.30
(`rp-23-34.pdf` p 16). The oracle comparison is
`make difftest SCOPE=student_loan_adjustment`; none of the 157 oracle
scenarios is inside a phase-out range, so the phase-out is tested only here and
by the Python cross-check recorded in the pull request.

> Using Types
> Using Student_loan_adjustment as S

## Wrapper with defaults

A wrapper gives each input a default: a single filer with $3,000 of qualifying
student loan interest, modified AGI of $70,000 (total income $70,000, no other
adjustments), not claimed as a dependent. Each test states only what it
changes. The defaults are satisfiable.

```catala
declaration scope Base:
  context filing_status content Types.FilingStatus
  context had_payments condition
  context loans_qualify condition
  context interest content money
  context is_mfj_dependent condition
  context claimed_as_dependent condition
  context total_income content money
  context other_adjustments content money
  s scope S.StudentLoanAdjustment
  output adjustment content money
  output phase_out content money
  output magi content money
  output cannot_deduct condition

scope Base:
  definition filing_status equals Single
  definition had_payments equals true
  definition loans_qualify equals true
  definition interest equals $3,000
  definition is_mfj_dependent equals false
  definition claimed_as_dependent equals false
  definition total_income equals $70,000
  definition other_adjustments equals $0
  definition s.filing_status equals filing_status
  definition s.had_student_loan_interest_payments equals had_payments
  definition s.student_loans_qualify equals loans_qualify
  definition s.student_loan_interest_amount equals interest
  definition s.is_mfj_dependent equals is_mfj_dependent
  definition s.either_filer_is_claimed_as_dependent equals claimed_as_dependent
  definition s.total_income equals total_income
  definition s.adjustments_to_income_excluding_student_loan_interest
    equals other_adjustments
  definition adjustment equals s.student_loan_interest_adjustment_amount
  definition phase_out equals s.student_loan_amount_phase_out_amount
  definition magi equals s.magi_for_student_loan_interest_deduction
  definition cannot_deduct equals s.cannot_deduct_student_loan_interest
```

## Acceptance cases

- $3,000 interest at MAGI $70,000, single: capped at $2,500, below the $80,000
  start, so $2,500.
- Single at MAGI $87,500: excess $7,500 over $15,000 is exactly one half
  (the ratio 0.500), so the phase-out is $1,250 and
  the deduction $1,250. The exact fraction gives the same.
- MFS: $0. MAGI $95,001 single: $0. MAGI $95,000 single: $0 (fully phased out,
  ratio 1.000). MFJ at MAGI $180,000: half of $2,500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStudentLoanCases:
  output ok condition
  below_range scope Base
  half_single scope Base
  mfs scope Base
  just_over scope Base
  at_end scope Base
  half_mfj scope Base
  at_start scope Base
  mfj_below scope Base
  other_adj scope Base

scope TestStudentLoanCases:
  rule ok fulfilled
  # defaults: single, interest $3,000, income $70,000
  definition half_single.total_income equals $87,500
  definition mfs.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition just_over.total_income equals $95,001
  definition at_end.total_income equals $95,000
  definition half_mfj.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition half_mfj.total_income equals $180,000
  definition at_start.total_income equals $80,000
  definition mfj_below.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_below.total_income equals $165,000
  # MAGI is total income less the other adjustments: $90,000 - $2,500 = $87,500
  definition other_adj.total_income equals $90,000
  definition other_adj.other_adjustments equals $2,500
  assertion below_range.adjustment = $2,500
  assertion half_single.phase_out = $1,250.00
  assertion half_single.adjustment = $1,250
  assertion mfs.adjustment = $0
  assertion mfs.cannot_deduct
  assertion just_over.adjustment = $0
  assertion just_over.cannot_deduct
  assertion at_end.adjustment = $0
  assertion not at_end.cannot_deduct
  assertion half_mfj.adjustment = $1,250
  assertion at_start.adjustment = $2,500
  assertion mfj_below.adjustment = $2,500
  assertion other_adj.magi = $87,500
  assertion other_adj.adjustment = $1,250
```

## DF-BUG(7): the exact fraction versus Direct File's three-decimal ratio

At MAGI $85,000 single the excess is $5,000 and the exact ratio is
0.33333...: the phase-out is $833.33 and the deduction
$2,500 - $833.33 = $1,666.67, which rounds to $1,667. Direct File rounds the
ratio to 0.333 and gets a phase-out of $832.50, deduction $1,668. The module
follows the statute (CONVENTIONS section 8); `df_phase_out_amount` reproduces
the Direct File number so the divergence is visible.

A tie case: for a joint return an excess of $15 over $165,000 gives
`10 x 15 / 30,000 = 0.005`, which `HALF_EVEN` rounds to 0.00, so Direct File
keeps the whole $2,500; the exact ratio 0.0005 gives $2,498.75, i.e. $2,499.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestThreeDecimalRatio:
  output ok condition
  third scope Base
  mfj_tie scope Base

scope TestThreeDecimalRatio:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition third.total_income equals $85,000
  definition mfj_tie.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_tie.total_income equals $165,015
  assertion third.phase_out = $833.33
  assertion third.adjustment = $1,667
  assertion S.exact_phase_out_amount of $5,000, $15,000, $2,500 = $833.33
  assertion S.df_phase_out_amount of $5,000, $15,000, $2,500 = $832.50
  assertion third.adjustment - $1,667 = $0
  # Direct File would give $1,668 here
  assertion not (third.adjustment = $1,668)
  assertion mfj_tie.adjustment = $2,499
  assertion S.df_phase_out_amount of $15, $30,000, $2,500 = $0.00
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.005 = $0.00
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.015 = $0.02
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.025 = $0.02
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.035 = $0.04
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.0049 = $0.00
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 0.0051 = $0.01
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of 1.0 = $1.00
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of (0.0 - 0.005) = $0.00
  assertion S.round_half_even_cents of (0.0 - 0.015) = (-$0.02)
```

## Eligibility

Claimed as a dependent, loans that do not qualify, no payments, and an MFJ
dependent each give $0. A qualifying MFJ filer with $500 of interest keeps it.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStudentLoanZero:
  output ok condition
  claimed scope Base
  not_qualifying scope Base
  no_payments scope Base
  mfj_dep scope Base
  small scope Base
  mfj_keeps scope Base

scope TestStudentLoanZero:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition claimed.claimed_as_dependent equals true
  definition not_qualifying.loans_qualify equals false
  # the amount box is filled in but the filer says there were no payments
  # (oracle ptc-no-aptc-negative-magi)
  definition no_payments.had_payments equals false
  definition mfj_dep.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_dep.is_mfj_dependent equals true
  definition small.interest equals $75
  definition mfj_keeps.filing_status equals MarriedFilingJointly
  definition mfj_keeps.interest equals $500
  assertion claimed.adjustment = $0
  assertion not_qualifying.adjustment = $0
  assertion no_payments.adjustment = $0
  assertion not no_payments.cannot_deduct
  assertion mfj_dep.adjustment = $0
  assertion small.adjustment = $75
  assertion mfj_keeps.adjustment = $500
```

## The spec rejects bad outputs

At MAGI $87,500 single the specification gives $1,250, so the capped $2,500
(phase-out forgotten) and $0 are rejected; likewise MFS must not get any
deduction and MAGI $95,001 must not get $2,500.

```catala
#[test]
declaration scope TestStudentLoanRejectsBad:
  output ok condition
  half_single scope Base
  mfs scope Base
  over scope Base

scope TestStudentLoanRejectsBad:
  rule ok fulfilled
  definition half_single.total_income equals $87,500
  definition mfs.filing_status equals MarriedFilingSeparately
  definition over.total_income equals $95,001
  assertion not (half_single.adjustment = $2,500)
  assertion not (half_single.adjustment = $0)
  assertion not (mfs.adjustment = $2,500)
  assertion not (over.adjustment = $2,500)
```
